{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement","id":805258,"title":"What do you want out of the next Demon Supplement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-10T08:20:05-08:00","id":805258,"title":"What do you want out of the next Demon Supplement","content":"(assuming there will be one at all, I've no idea if anything has been said).<br /> <br /> Contracts: I know they've been covered in DtD and Players guide, but I still feel like some parts aren't greatly covered. Like the sell... or some of the nitty gritty of what happens on collect. How demons deal with contracts that aren't straight forward. How they research and approach victims. Probably just because I'm not a good sales person, I don't understand outside of embedding weird shit in legalese that no one reads how they ever get anyone to sign.<br /> <br /> Cults: God Machine and Demon, what do they look like? how do they behave? Actually I might be happy to have an entire book on ChroD cults, seeing as how Vampires and other things have them too.<br /> <br /> Religious Undertones: This kind of ties into cults, but as mentioned in a different thread, DtD doesn't always feel religious, getting into it with cults might be enough, but more advice on how to give it this feel would be good. On this note describing more of how the unchained seem like devils to people would be good. To me I can't even imagine (outside of propaganda) why they'd appear evil, nor do I see their motivation to be evil. also appearance, like why would a demon end up looking big and red with horns? I know you can do all of this, I'd just like to see more of *how*.<br /> <br /> what do you want to see in the next supplement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 01-10-2016, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T11:09:48-08:00","id":805357,"title":"","content":"I am, in general, supporting these topics for expansion as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement#post805258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me I can't even imagine (outside of propaganda) why they'd appear evil, nor do I see their motivation to be evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for reasons people are leery of Demons: Many are unashamedly assholes. They're liars. They use people like pawn and shields. Unlike many other supernaturals, they were never human, nor do they really seek to be.<br /> <br /> As for the Demon's motivation: &quot;Needs must&quot;. Life living a lie is tough, and sometimes you have to ruin a few lives if you are going to survive. The Demon's that don't/can't make those choices? Usually end up recycled in short order.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T11:39:28-08:00","id":805377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement?p=805357#post805357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am, in general, supporting these topics for expansion as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for reasons people are leery of Demons: Many are unashamedly assholes. They're liars. They use people like pawn and shields. Unlike many other supernaturals, they were never human, nor do they really seek to be.<br /> <br /> As for the Demon's motivation: &quot;Needs must&quot;. Life living a lie is tough, and sometimes you have to ruin a few lives if you are going to survive. The Demon's that don't/can't make those choices? Usually end up recycled in short order.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> right and maybe some of my perspective on the problem is the game doesn't discuss the fallout of a contract very much. Seems to me like people forget they &quot;had relationship&quot;, nobody is the wiser that the demon replaced someone. I'm sure people get hurt but I feel like the how seems very subtle, to the point where it's hard to be aware of it. It's not obviously like vampires who drain people and leave bodies, or werewolves going on a warpath.<br /> <br /> Maybe the book should be about &quot;human interactions with demons/gm&quot; I feel that's like 90% of what I'm missing. Because, the religious aspect is more of a human perception thing I think (I doubt demons/GM see it that way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T11:57:46-08:00","id":805385,"title":"","content":"Depends: are there expanded rules for boltholes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T13:35:27-08:00","id":805446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement#post805258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(assuming there will be one at all, I've no idea if anything has been said).<br /> <br /> On this note describing more of how the unchained seem like devils to people would be good. To me I can't even imagine (outside of propaganda) why they'd appear evil, nor do I see their motivation to be evil. also appearance, like why would a demon end up looking big and red with horns? I know you can do all of this, I'd just like to see more of *how*.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mortal Remains (Hunter supplement) has a really good examination of Demons in mortal perception.<br /> <br /> &quot;Outside of propaganda&quot; is a bit of an understatement. The G_m has had thousands of years of human civilization to sell the &quot;Demons = bad&quot; bit. Add to the fact that the mere act of <i>explaining</i> the truth to a mortal friend or loved one triggers a compromise and puts them in harms way doesn't allow much opportunity to tell the other side of the story. Given their ability to perfectly lie and conceal (or fake) their emotion, trust relationships between fellow unchained can take decades to build, and can be lost in a single instant. Heck I think five pages into the opening fiction of the core Kyle and Mr. Knight discuss the impact that Demon trust issue have, and how it detracts from accomplishing what they need to do.<br /> <br /> That and they sell souls, which is kind of a negative as far as most are concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T14:30:00-08:00","id":805494,"title":"","content":"CofD needs a general book on Cults; Vampire, Mage, Changeling, Hunter, Mummy, and Demon could all easily use those rules to great effect.<br /> <br /> Honestly, all I really want out of DtD at this point is more Dark Eras. I'm hoping the Fall of Constantinople will give me what I need to run a Renaissance Italy game of Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:25:19-08:00","id":805537,"title":"","content":"Back to the original post topic:<br /> <br /> More blue book support for the GMC's line. As is, the G-M is tightly tied to DtD, and given the discussion that ran in the general Chronicles of Darkness, not much anywhere else. I have the feeling that the more people are interested in GMC, the more support can be justified for Demon the Descent.<br /> <br /> A cryptid book (preferably a blue book for reasons above): Go whole-hog with this: Cryptoflora, albino alligators, men in black (angels in disguise, simularca, mass hallucinations?), UFO sightings, bigfoot, loch ness, etc.<br /> <br /> A Deva Corporation Sourcebook. Someone floated the idea of devoting few pages to support Deva as a Hunter conspiracy, complete with reverse engineered G-M and Demon tech. I think that's an excellent idea. Also throw in new gadgets, how the Deva corp operates, what the management factions are, what the corporate culture is like, and what the security challenges are in infiltrating it. The Deva Corporation should <b><i>not</i></b> be a retread of Pentex. The more plausible the Deva corporation is, the more chilling. These are people committed to a new future and a new vision of humanity. If they need to vivisect demons or harvest brain tissue from fractals, so be it, that's not any worse than outsourcing to Chinese factories where children work 16 hour days making computer chips for your smart phone.<br /> <br /> A Nighthorrors book for DtD: Sleepers, stigmatics, cryptids, cults, simularca, rival demons, Angels, Exiles, Slivers and Facilities. Nighthorrors is an excellent line that has knocked it out of the park every time. Let's have one for Demon.<br /> <br /> A Nighthorrors Book for Tokyo: Imagine your ring chased down the back streets of Tokyo by a vengeful Inugami, bargaining for your child's life with Kuchisake-Onna, investigating a derelict school that could well be an abandoned Infrastructure. Make it a blue book for cross-over with Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> A Book of Incarnations: A book discussing incarnations more rules hacks and resources . Here's the hook: make it for both angels and demons. New embeds and exploits for demons, new numina and incepts for angels and exiles. Incarnation specific merits, etc, etc,<br /> <br /> More City settings. Specifically, city books that are the equal of Splintered City Seattle. Seattle is a science-fiction-horror wonderland: Time travel reminiscent of Chrono Trigger, corporate conspiracies and cool places like the Apocalypse Vault. The cities in the seed collection were cool, and had great ideas, but were a little sparse as a result of the limited word count.<br /> <br /> Travel in the GMC. think Midnight Roads, but more aimed at planes, trains and automobiles. How do you move about in world that's monitored by biomechanical horrors? Specific advice for running a Tier-3 Agency with global responsibilities. Also a generic Airport that Storytellers can incorporate into their cities a la Tales from the 13th Precinct, with locations, a dozen alphabet soup government agencies, storyteller characters, secrets and mysteries and advice for making it a convert battleground between the Unchained and the G-M's angels.<br /> <br /> (meanwhile, the devs are looking at this and thinking &quot;He does realize that we have about a dozen game lines we need to publish for, right?&quot;)<br /> <br /> Edit: A Book of Splinters, may that we can mix and match for whatever city our chronicle is based in, maybe some overlap with Dark Eras (1950s Berlins where the Nazi party managed to survive via negotiated surrender perhaps? One where the Soviets took the city completely?) Future Splinters (cyberpuk ho!), past splinters, alternate timelines etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 01-17-2016, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:35:25-08:00","id":805546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement?p=805377#post805377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">right and maybe some of my perspective on the problem is the game doesn't discuss the fallout of a contract very much. Seems to me like people forget they &quot;had relationship&quot;, nobody is the wiser that the demon replaced someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody <i>immediately concerned with the pacted party</i> is the wiser, which tends to have knock-on effects when dealing with anyone who knows people who don't know the pactbound. Your mark's mother-in-law is going to be a problem, for example.<br /> <br /> There's also the problem of demonic stealth not being perfect by any stretch; an unbreakable poker face doesn't protect you from errors in judgment, much less resolve the little occult stress-fractures that investigators find to degrade your Cover. Things don't add up around the Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:52:44-08:00","id":805556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement?p=805537#post805537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cryptid book (preferably a blue book for reasons above): Go whole-hog with this: Cryptoflora, albino alligators, men in black (angels in disguise, simularca, mass hallucinations?), UFO sightings, bigfoot, loch ness, etc.<br /> <br /> A Nighthorrors book for DtD: Sleepers, stigmatics, Cryptids, cults, simularca, rival demons, Angels, Exiles, Slivers and Facilities. Nighthorrors is an excellent line that has knocked it out of the park every time. Let's have one for Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally adore either of these. As much as I'd love a little book of cryptids (with lots of new Adaptations, diverse sample cryptids and cryptoflora and a Shard focusing on human cryptid-hunters), the Night Horrors book is probably the better call; I'd be amazed if a cryptid or two didn't sneak into it and I'd love to make up some new Tools of the Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:46:20-08:00","id":805756,"title":"","content":"Any CofD book that dedicated a decent amount of wordcount to UFO and how they relate to the setting would be an instant buy for me.<br /> <br /> I don't want space aliens, mind you. I just want more High Weirdness unrelated to the greater setting at large; sure, throw out the possibility of odd Angels, Qashmallim, spirits, or odd things from the Astral, but leave them largely weird and unexplained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:04:13-08:00","id":805936,"title":"","content":"A Night Horrors book and something about Tokyo are both things I support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:39:08-08:00","id":805955,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd really love to see some Demon fiction released, although I'm not sure if that's ever going to be a possibility for the business model. A Demon novel would be great though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:41:51-08:00","id":806114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement?p=805756#post805756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any CofD book that dedicated a decent amount of wordcount to UFO and how they relate to the setting would be an instant buy for me.<br /> <br /> I don't want space aliens, mind you. I just want more High Weirdness unrelated to the greater setting at large; sure, throw out the possibility of odd Angels, Qashmallim, spirits, or odd things from the Astral, but leave them largely weird and unexplained.</div> </div> </div> </div>As ever, we are the same person","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:25:06-08:00","id":806262,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a Night Horrors deck of cards for Demon: the Descent containing cryptids, Angels, Exiles, Imperatives, and even Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T19:46:13-08:00","id":806689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement?p=805756#post805756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any CofD book that dedicated a decent amount of wordcount to UFO and how they relate to the setting would be an instant buy for me.<br /> <br /> I don't want space aliens, mind you. I just want more High Weirdness unrelated to the greater setting at large; sure, throw out the possibility of odd Angels, Qashmallim, spirits, or odd things from the Astral, but leave them largely weird and unexplained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. The G-m Phenomena section from the Urban Legends chapter was my favorite pleasant surprise in the STG. You can drop them in any city you care to mention to make it Seattle level <i>weird</i>. That alone was worth the price of admission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:44:35-08:00","id":808030,"title":"","content":"I think a Night Horrors style book would make a lot of sense, IMO. One with more weird GM phenomena, Angels, Exiles and some weird Demons. That would be rad as heck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:15:03-08:00","id":808325,"title":"","content":"Incepts that affect and interact with an Angel's influences. I get off on terrifying my players. I might have a problem.<br /> <br /> Splintered City: New Dehli. A massive urban area that's home of the Deva Corporation and the Pain Prophet. The nearby Chinese and Pakistani borders mean that mundane espionage is rampant, as is cyber-espionage. The chance to see the G-M through a different cultural lens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T04:42:30-08:00","id":810175,"title":"","content":"If we're voting, yes, Night Horrors.<br /> <br /> I'd love an entry on &quot;legend has it, a really power piece of Infrastructure somehow 'gained sentience' and 'went rogue.' It currently plans to demolish the G-M, once it gains enough power. By the way, the power it needs to consume... is Primum.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4576-darthdoctor","name":"DarthDoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T05:07:43-08:00","id":810179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement?p=805537#post805537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the original post topic:<br /> <br /> More blue book support for the GMC's line. As is, the G-M is tightly tied to DtD, and given the discussion that ran in the general Chronicles of Darkness, not much anywhere else. I have the feeling that the more people are interested in GMC, the more support can be justified for Demon the Descent.<br /> <br /> A cryptid book (preferably a blue book for reasons above): Go whole-hog with this: Cryptoflora, albino alligators, men in black (angels in disguise, simularca, mass hallucinations?), UFO sightings, bigfoot, loch ness, etc.<br /> <br /> A Deva Corporation Sourcebook. Someone floated the idea of devoting few pages to support Deva as a Hunter conspiracy, complete with reverse engineered G-M and Demon tech. I think that's an Excellent idea. Also throw in new gadgets, how the Deva corp operates, what the management factions are, what the corporate culture is like, and what the security challenges are in infiltrating it. The Deva Corporation should <b><i>not</i></b> be a retread of Pentex. The more plausible the Deva corporation is, the more chilling. These are people committed to a new future and a new vision of humanity. If they need to vivisect demons or harvest brain tissue from fractals, so be it, that's not any worse than outsourcing to Chinese factories where children work 16 hour days making computer chips for your smart phone.<br /> <br /> A Nighthorrors book for DtD: Sleepers, stigmatics, cryptids, cults, simularca, rival demons, Angels, Exiles, Slivers and Facilities. Nighthorrors is an excellent line that has knocked it out of the park every time. Let's have one for Demon.<br /> <br /> A Nighthorrors Book for Tokyo: Imagine your ring chased down the back streets of Tokyo by a vengeful Inugami, bargaining for your child's life with Kuchisake-Onna, investigating a derelict school that could well be an abandoned Infrastructure. Make it a blue book for cross-over with Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> A Book of Incarnations: A book discussing incarnations more rules hacks and resources . Here's the hook: make it for both angels and demons. New embeds and exploits for demons, new numina and incepts for angels and exiles. Incarnation specific merits, etc, etc,<br /> <br /> More City settings. Specifically, city books that are the equal of Splintered City Seattle. Seattle is a science-fiction-horror wonderland: Time travel reminiscent of Chrono Trigger, corporate conspiracies and cool places like the Apocalypse Vault. The cities in the seed collection were cool, and had great ideas, but were a little sparse as a result of the limited word count.<br /> <br /> Travel in the GMC. think Midnight Roads, but more aimed at planes, trains and automobiles. How do you move about in world that's monitored by biomechanical horrors? Specific advice for running a Tier-3 Agency with global responsibilities. Also a generic Airport that Storytellers can incorporate into their cities a la Tales from the 13th Precinct, with locations, a dozen alphabet soup government agencies, storyteller characters, secrets and mysteries and advice for making it a convert battleground between the Unchained and the G-M's angels.<br /> <br /> (meanwhile, the devs are looking at this and thinking &quot;He does realize that we have about a dozen game lines we need to publish for, right?&quot;)<br /> <br /> Edit: A Book of Splinters, may that we can mix and match for whatever city our chronicle is based in, maybe some overlap with Dark Eras (1950s Berlins where the Nazi party managed to survive via negotiated surrender perhaps? One where the Soviets took the city completely?) Future Splinters (cyberpuk ho!), past splinters, alternate timelines etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would love books for all of this.<br /> <br /> I really want a book on NYC. There is so much they could do with it.NYC has the UN in it wich makes me think that NYC is the opposite of Seattle. The God machine has insane amounts of control here and even looking at it from above Manhattan looks like a chip<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/9c4KG_8iTZM?t=55s\" data-code=\"9c4KG_8iTZM\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9c4KG_8iTZM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Skip to 55 second<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I would love to see a book on just more interesting infrastructures<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh also more embeds,exploits and gadgets.<br /> <br /> Also more god machine weirdness would be interesting. Such as what if demons found the god machine has infrastructure on the moon or god forbid mars or something.<br /> <br /> If they will not put out an NYC book I guess I could just write it up and post it on the Forum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 01-16-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T07:01:14-08:00","id":810212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement?p=808325#post808325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incepts that affect and interact with an Angel's influences. I get off on terrifying my players. I might have a problem.<br /> <br /> Splintered City: New Dehli. A massive urban area that's home of the Deva Corporation and the Pain Prophet. The nearby Chinese and Pakistani borders mean that mundane espionage is rampant, as is cyber-espionage. The chance to see the G-M through a different cultural lens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> more on Deva would definitely be nice too, I forgot about that (though perhaps falls under my &quot;more on cults&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T22:20:58-08:00","id":825278,"title":"","content":"A Deviant: the ??? and Altered State Cross-over setting.<br /> <br /> Altered States presents a monolithic surveillance-state dystopia under the control of a deity that uses the population as a combination of cattle and lab rats. AS did a fabulous job of cramming a setting, character creation rules and a few plot seed into 11 pages, but damn if I didn\u2019t want more.<br /> <br /> Deviant is (will be) a setting about victims of an experiment gone horribly wrong, rebelling against the organization that created them.<br /> <br /> Chocolate, meet my good friend peanut butter, I\u2019m sure you two will get along.<br /> <br /> Deviants would fit right in as antagonists to the SOE (who are called upon to deal with other things besides demons) and as protagonists in and of their own right. Flung out into the street with few resources, or even much knowledge with what's going on, they work either as reluctant heroes who are forced to oppose the system, or as tragic villains that the SOE has to track and put down.<br /> <br /> Demons in this setting work little differently, they\u2019ve had more time to prepare and accumulate resources. SOE are outsiders, but they\u2019re working for the G-M.<br /> <br /> Following on the toolbox approach of CoD, it would be trivially easy to use the expanded material for a dedicated SOE chronicle without Deviant. Topics to include:<br /> <br /> The resistance:<br /> How it operates in a state under the control of an ascendant super-computer and it\u2019s agents.<br /> Endowments. The resistance has had years of technognostic revelations from fallen angels. They\u2019ve had the time to put together some sort of equalizer, not to mention the stock piles of gadgets that past demons have gifted to them.<br /> How they interact with they\u2019re demonic patrons. Demons in this shard are even more calculating than the norm. They have to be. They\u2019ve had the opportunity to calculate, and prepare for their fall, they\u2019ve had the time to assemble resources. And if they need a new identity, is a patch job really a possibility? In a world where everything is indexed and controlled? Or is a Soul-Pact the only true option a demon has to hide from it\u2019s. Additionally there\u2019s the logical parallel of the SOE organized around an angelic master, and a resistance cell organized around a demonic master.<br /> <br /> The SOE:<br /> More Tech, story seeds, some sample NPCs (Stigmatic and angels).<br /> <br /> The Setting:<br /> C\u2019mon. Do it. Chronicles of Darkness does a full-on techno-gnostic dystopian cyberpunk? You know you want it. From loyal followers of the G-M, to criminals (every society has them), to the resistance, to counter-cultural groups, what\u2019s it like to live in a world where the Machine provides everything except freedom?<br /> <br /> Additionally: If we do get a night horrors book: let\u2019s have 2-4 entries that are native to Altered State. Say an Exile that\u2019s found his (or her) way out of the Mechopolis into the real world and wants to get back\u2026 or create it in the real world. The <i>entire</i> world. Also, a semi-mythical slasher that operates in Mechopolis, a spook story, officially denied, that SOE operative tell each other on slow nights around the water cooler.<br /> <br /> If we get a Cryptids books, have it devote 10-14 pages to an Ozarks Seed, a la the rest of the Demon Seed collection. Demon is usually urban-based, but the wealth of cryptids in Ozark mythology is too good not to make an exception. Plus the wealth of Cryptids in the area means there must be a glut of Infrastructure in the area, with agencies competing to subvert them.<br /> <br /> Also: a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NXrmRW_v1s8\" target=\"_blank\">Hide-Behind</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 02-07-2016, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}